WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.451
Modernization programs spend most
of their attention on day one:

2
00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:08.037
the tenant is built, identities
sync, the cutover runs.

3
00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:11.809
But the estate is judged on
day two, when every reset,

4
00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:14.862
unlock and new hire
lands at the help desk.

5
00:00:14.862 --> 00:00:17.913
In Entra ID the help desk's power is real.

6
00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:21.526
Microsoft calls the Helpdesk
Administrator role privileged,

7
00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:26.251
and warns that changing a user's password
can mean taking over that user's identity.

8
00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:30.068
Forcing MFA re-registration
wipes the user's methods,

9
00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:33.625
and whoever registers next
controls the account.

10
00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:37.850
So a reset on an unverified
request isn't a support task.

11
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.350
It's handing the account to whoever asked.

12
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.369
Attackers know this; CISA
has described groups

13
00:00:43.369 --> 00:00:46.238
that talked help desk
staff into exactly that.

14
00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:49.837
And when the governed path is
hard, the desk works around it.

15
00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:52.800
Next, what federal guidance
says about recovery.
